window.KINTSU_DOCS_INDEX = [{"page":"docs.html","title":"Kintsu documentation","heading":"","id":"","text":"Install, keys, configuration, questions, roadmap. One page each."},{"page":"docs.html","title":"Kintsu documentation","heading":"Design documents","id":"design","text":"In the repository. They are the reference if this site and the code disagree. VISION.md — The problem, the existing tools, the roadmap ARCHITECTURE.md — Entities, use cases, adapters DAEMON.md — The resident process MODELS.md — Several models, one per task UI.md — The bubble CONTRIBUTING.md — How to contribute"},{"page":"install.html","title":"Install","heading":"","id":"","text":"One static binary. No runtime, no account."},{"page":"install.html","title":"Install","heading":"One line","id":"one-line","text":"macOS · Linux · zsh, bash, fish today Installs the binary in ~/.local/bin and asks before adding one line to your shell configuration. Open a new shell. Done."},{"page":"install.html","title":"Install","heading":"If you skipped the hook","id":"hook","text":"Add the line yourself, then open a new shell. zsh bash fish ~/.zshrc ~/.bashrc In bash, messages arrive at the next prompt and there is no ghost text. Everything else is the same. ~/.config/fish/config.fish"},{"page":"install.html","title":"Install","heading":"Other ways","id":"other","text":"Package managers arrive with v0.1. Building from source works today. macOS Linux From source Servers, tmux, Herdr Homebrew with v0.1 or prebuilt binary with v0.1 Intel Macs: x86_64-apple-darwin . prebuilt binary with v0.1 Static build, any distribution. aarch64 too. or cargo binstall with v0.1 or Nix, AUR later, help w"},{"page":"install.html","title":"Install","heading":"Uninstall","id":"uninstall","text":"removes the binary and the hook line Nothing else was touched."},{"page":"install.html","title":"Install","heading":"Installer options","id":"options","text":"For automation, a custom directory, or a shell you manage yourself. --dir DIR install directory; default ~/.local/bin , or $KINTSU_INSTALL_DIR --no-hook do not edit any shell configuration file --yes add the hook without asking; also KINTSU_YES=1 --version vX.Y.Z a specific release instead of the latest --from-source s"},{"page":"install.html","title":"Install","heading":"After v0.1","id":"next","text":"Three commands come with the first release: kintsu setup writes the configuration, kintsu doctor checks it, kintsu service install keeps the daemon running after logout."},{"page":"keys.html","title":"Keys and commands","heading":"","id":"","text":"Every action has a key, a clickable word and a command. The single letters work once the panel is open."},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"","id":"","text":"~/.config/kintsu/config.toml , written by kintsu setup , checked by kintsu doctor , overridden per project by a .kintsu.toml at the root of a repository. This is the planned schema; it may change until v0.1 ships, and every change will be listed in the changelog."},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Models","id":"models","text":"A model is a named endpoint: a provider, a model id, how to reach it, what it may be used for. Name them the way you will read them in kintsu models : tiny , haiku , local-big , work . [models.<name>] provider covers needs where ollama any model Ollama serves; health and listing through the native API Ollama running lo"},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Routing","id":"routing","text":"Five tasks. For each, an ordered list of model names. The router takes the first candidate the constraints allow and that is not in a failed state (circuit breaker); on a timeout or an error it moves to the next. rules-only is a pseudo-model meaning \"do without a model\" and every list ends with it whether you write it "},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Constraints","id":"constraints","text":"Constraints filter the candidate lists before the router selects one. They keep a case containing a secret away from cloud models and enforce the budget. [routing.constraints] constraint value effect sensitive_output \"local_only\" · \"ask\" · \"allow\" default local_only . ask shows the Privacy tab before any cloud call. of"},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Keys","id":"keys","text":"A key source, per model, in order of preference. The daemon reads keys once, keeps them in memory, never logs them, never puts them in the protocol. keychain environment variable command literal key = { … } macOS Keychain or Linux secret-service. Stored by kintsu login <model> . key = { … } Read from the daemon's envir"},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Agents","id":"agents","text":"Presets define how the brief is passed to each CLI. A template covers any other command. {brief} is the path of the Markdown brief Kintsu wrote; {brief_text} inlines it. [models.<agent>] preset runs claude claude \"$(cat {brief})\" , or claude -p when open_in = \"print\" codex codex \"$(cat {brief})\" , or codex exec for pri"},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"The bubble","id":"ui","text":"[ui]"},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Noise","id":"noise","text":"[quiet] At the prompt: kintsu ignore with --command , --dir , --session or --always ; kintsu mute 1h ; KINTSU_DISABLE=1 to disable the hook in one shell."},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Daemon and hooks","id":"daemon","text":"[daemon] kintsu service install writes a LaunchAgent on macOS and a user unit on Linux so the daemon keeps running after logout and restarts after a crash. Without it, the daemon starts on the first failure after login."},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Per project","id":"project","text":"A .kintsu.toml at the root of a repository overrides the user file for cases whose cwd is inside it. Anything can be overridden; these are the ones that make sense to commit. .kintsu.toml"},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Complete examples","id":"examples","text":"Local only One key Your subscription At work local only: Ollama, nothing is sent local one key: Haiku for explanations, tiny for classification cloud local no key at all: your Claude Code subscription your account at work: an approved endpoint, private paths, a budget cloud"},{"page":"configuration.html","title":"Configuration","heading":"Commands that touch the configuration","id":"commands","text":"kintsu setup three questions, writes the file, offers service install kintsu doctor parses the file, probes every model, prints what works, what is missing and what an answer would cost kintsu models the table: name, provider, tier, where, health, latency, today's cost kintsu models test [name] sends a tiny prompt and "},{"page":"faq.html","title":"FAQ","heading":"","id":"","text":"Twenty-four questions in five groups. Missing one? Open an issue ."},{"page":"roadmap.html","title":"Roadmap","heading":"","id":"","text":"No dates. A version ships when every item in its list works."},{"page":"roadmap.html","title":"Roadmap","heading":"Hooks and design","id":"the-skeleton","text":"now  Hooks for zsh, bash and fish Design documents: architecture, daemon, models, UI The installer and this site v0.1 The bubble Goal: a suggestion is shown under every failed command. Daemon: one process per user, Unix socket, started on demand Rule engine: command typos, wrong directory, git, Docker not running, port"}];
